   memory/sm2.js          the SM-2 scheduler as a memory driver
   aperture/              /pick/*, /review/literal, /preview/literal
-dataset/                 @anki/topography/latin-core
+dataset/                 @memoriter/topography/latin-core
   latin.viva.js          DATASET + FRAUGHT: seeds on daemon boot, serves freight
   entities/              219 words, 50 sentences, ~240 symbols, built by build.js
   freight/               10 voices (sentences), 10 pictures (nouns) — placeholders
-mode/                    @anki/srs/anki — the one mode
-  anki.viva.js           APPLICATION STANDALONE EMITTER EXPOSED HARNESSED CONVERSATIONAL TOOLED
-  buffer/Anki.svelte     the tablet: flip, four grades with live SM-2 horizons
+mode/                    @memoriter/srs/memoriter — the one mode
+  memoriter.viva.js      APPLICATION STANDALONE EMITTER EXPOSED HARNESSED CONVERSATIONAL TOOLED
+  buffer/Memoriter.svelte  the tablet: flip, four grades with live SM-2 horizons
   harness.js + hal/      Magister, the persona
   tools/                 /review /grade /memory /add — the conversational loop
   aperture.js            /chat (harness render) and /stats
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ English to Latin, classical and ecclesiastical. Ten topics from Religio to Sermo
 Registered like any out-of-tree package: the folder's absolute path appended to `testament/ledger/registry.json`, the daemon declared in the variant:
 
 ```js
-kernel: ["@anki/domain/srs", "@anki/topography/latin-core", "@anki/srs/anki"]
+kernel: ["@memoriter/domain/srs", "@memoriter/topography/latin-core", "@memoriter/srs/memoriter"]
 ```
 
 The one imported registry module is the hallucinator (`@viva/hallucinator/anthropic`), which powers the Magister's conversation; everything else the package carries.
